cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below, together with the 4DGS methods whose outputs you view."
title: "gs4d_viewer: One Representation and One Viewer for the Outputs of 4D Gaussian Splatting Methods"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Luu
    given-names: Thai Cong
repository-code: "https://github.com/zerokhong1/gs4d_viewer"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  gs4d_viewer converts the trained output of 4D Gaussian Splatting methods (per-frame Gaussians, 4D Gaussians sliced in time,
  parametric motion functions and neural deformation fields) into one representation, the Gaussians at a set of keyframes with
  linear interpolation in between, by re-implementing each method's evaluation at time t on the CPU. One renderer then displays
  every method under the same camera and time controls. The conversion is validated against the methods' own renderers on the
  same images.
keywords:
  - 4D Gaussian Splatting
  - dynamic scenes
  - novel view synthesis
  - visualization
